-- Trace data foundation v2.26.0: Phase 4 remediation content (D31-D36): pm-bridges-v2, pm-actions-v2, pm-eligibility-v2.
-- GENERATED by scripts/build_transition_content.py from the reviewed JSON files. Do not edit by hand; edit the JSON
-- and regenerate. Earlier versions (pm-bridges-v1, pm-actions-v1, pm-eligibility-v1) are kept unchanged for audit.
-- D32/D34: Each bridge separates source facts (responsibilities, levels, stated entry requirements) from Trace's curated reading (which pack requirements it develops fully or partly) and from hypotheses (transitions no cited source establishes). Partial development never closes a gap (D32): each partial requirement states what the bridge develops, what remains incomplete and what responsibility to seek. Program Manager is not a bridge (D27). Product Owner is alternative-only (D34).
-- D33: D33: the digital roles F1 explicitly lists as sharing product manager skills ('Roles that share product manager skills'), under their original names. A candidate pool only: none is an approved bridge. Ambiguous mappings are left unmapped.
-- D28: Templates are instantiated per requirement from the user's own assessment: Gap -> Build (stage 1) and Demonstrate (stage 2); Transferable -> Demonstrate (stage 2) and Reposition (stage 3); Demonstrated -> Reposition (stage 3) only; Unknown -> resolve the missing information first (stage 0), no capability action. Stage 4 is always considered. No courses, providers, costs, timelines, placement outcomes or job openings are named or implied; current openings come only from verified postings in the knowledge base. Revision v2: learning exercises and personal projects are labelled; repositioning keeps to confirmed records; skill and role-history evidence have their own reposition templates; Stage 4 adds employer criteria, a case study, case practice, alternative routes and, on bridge routes, the responsibility still to seek.
-- D36: Structure preserves AND (all) / OR (any), ranges and required versus preferred. Leaves: years_in_families (reviewed roles in the named role families, from partial dates: 'meets' only when the certain minimum reaches the stated minimum, 'does not meet' only when the possible maximum cannot), product_exposure (confirmed, categorised responsibility evidence in a role of the named families showing a product-ownership area; a job title alone never counts), current_role_in_families and not_transitioning_from (the user's CURRENT confirmed role only; earlier roles never trigger an exclusion), total_years, qualification (an 'or equivalent' clause never gives 'does not meet'; a missing qualification record is unclear, never absence), and stated_condition (a condition the profile cannot show, such as a product domain; always unclear). Preferred criteria are reported but never decide the outcome. Revision v2 (D36): product management tenure leaves list Product Owner and founder families as possible equivalents, which give Unclear (never meets or does not meet on their own); qualifications match the stated field on normalised whole values through explicit aliases, or a degree type (B.E./B.Tech); internships, part-time work and apprenticeships with an unspecified work pattern never count towards the certain minimum.
-- Curated public reference content: no user data, no synthetic test data.

